<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
                   xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                   xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
                                       http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-3.6.xsd">

    <!--
      2026-09-27 — the audit trail says what each row records.

      lc-muw-2026-06-02-audit-event-type-display-names.xml gave the heritage
      types human labels, but from id 9 onwards many of them were shifted off
      the meaning the database triggers write them with. The live
      study_event trigger writes 24 when a visit's start date changes, and
      the log called that "Study event reset"; 19 (visit completed) read
      "Study event location updated", 21 (visit skipped) read "Study event
      started", 27 (subject moved to another site) read "Discrepancy note
      added". The recorded rows were always right. Only the labels were
      wrong, and in an audit trail a wrong label misstates what happened.

      The first changeset puts every affected label back on the meaning its
      writer gives it: the event_crf, study_event, study_subject and
      repeating item_data triggers (latest definitions in 3.8, amethyst and
      3.6). No audit row is touched; the label is looked up, not copied.

      Two ids were also being written by MUW code with the old, wrong meaning:
      11 for reopening and for restoring a CRF, and 27 for a reason-for-change
      note. Those writers get types of their own (138-140), and the audit view
      maps rows written before this change by what they record (table and
      column marker) rather than by id alone. 137 gives restoring a dismissed
      file its own type; it was written under 128 and read as a dismissal.
    -->
    <changeSet id="2026-12-08-audit-type-labels-heritage-meaning" author="muw">
        <update tableName="audit_log_event_type">
            <column name="display_name" value="CRF interview details changed"/>
            <where>audit_log_event_type_id = 9</where>
        </update>
        <update tableName="audit_log_event_type">
            <column name="display_name" value="CRF initial data entry completed"/>
            <where>audit_log_event_type_id = 10</where>
        </update>
        <update tableName="audit_log_event_type">
            <column name="display_name" value="CRF double data entry completed"/>
            <where>audit_log_event_type_id = 11</where>
        </update>
        <update tableName="audit_log_event_type">
            <column name="display_name" value="CRF marked complete with e-signature"/>
            <where>audit_log_event_type_id = 14</where>
        </update>
        <update tableName="audit_log_event_type">
            <column name="display_name" value="CRF initial data entry completed with e-signature"/>
